# Security

- Authenticate on the server. Authorize every API mutation.
- Before a read or write, verify resource ownership or an explicit role permission (`STUDENT`, `MENTOR`, `ADMIN`).
- Validate and authorize on the server. Client checks are not the boundary.
- Hash passwords with a strong one-way algorithm. Never store or log plaintext passwords.
- Secrets live in env or the platform secret store. Never commit them.
- Never put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (those values ship to the browser).
- GitHub PATs stay on the server. Do not return the token, a prefix, or any field that contains it.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — token reaches the client
return { githubToken: process.env.GITHUB_PAT };

// ✅ GOOD — server uses the token; client gets only public data
const pull = await github.getPullRequest(id);
return { number: pull.number, title: pull.title };
```
